Architecture
============

Project Layout
--------------
dumpware/
├── go.mod
├── README / LICENSE / SECURITY / CODE_OF_CONDUCT
├── docs/                      # you are here
│
├── i18n/
│   ├── i18n.go               # loads + serves translations
│   └── locales/*.json         # one file per language
│
└── src/
    ├── main.go                 # ties everything together
    ├── system/
    │   ├── os.go                # OS enum + detection (runtime.GOOS)
    │   └── packagemanager.go    # package manager enum + detection
    ├── catalog/
    │   ├── types.go             # Category, Item, InstallCommand
    │   └── data.go               # the actual catalog content
    ├── wizard/
    │   └── wizard.go             # all terminal prompts
    └── installer/
        ├── installer.go          # runs the install commands
        ├── util.go                # shared download/exec helpers
        ├── windows_php.go         # special-cased PHP install on Windows
        ├── linux_mullvad.go       # special-cased Mullvad on Apt/Dnf
        └── linux_ventoy.go        # special-cased Ventoy on Linux


Package Breakdown
-----------------

system
------
Two small enums with detection logic attached.

- OS (MacOS, Linux, Windows, Unknown) DetectOS() reads runtime.GOOS.
- PackageManager (Apt, Dnf, Pacman, Zypper, Apk, Xbps)
  DetectPackageManagers() checks exec.LookPath for each candidate
  binary and returns whichever ones actually exist on the machine.

Nothing here touches the catalog or the wizard--it only answers
"what am I running on".

catalog
-------
Pure data, no logic beyond a lookup.

- Item describes one installable thing: an ID, a display name, a
  description key (for i18n), and one InstallCommand per platform
  (a map keyed by PackageManager for Linux, since that varies).
- Category groups items under a translated name (NameKey).
- Item.CommandFor(os, pm) returns the right InstallCommand for the
  current OS/PM combo, or ok = false if there isn't one.
- catalog.All() in data.go is the single source of truth for every
  category and item Dumpware knows about.

wizard
------
Everything that talks to the terminal lives here. Nowhere else reads
or writes stdin/stdout directly except this package and installer.go
(which streams subprocess output).

- SelectLanguage, SelectOS, SelectPackageManager, SelectItems,
  Confirm — each one prints a prompt, reads a line, and parses it
  (by index or by name, whichever makes sense).
- Falls back to sane defaults whenever input is empty or invalid
  (detected OS, first available package manager, etc).

installer
---------
Takes the final selection and executes it.

- Install() loops over selected items, resolves the right command via
  Item.CommandFor, and runs it with stdout/stderr/stdin wired straight
  to the terminal so the user sees native install output live.
- On Windows it first tries winget source update (best effort, logs
  a warning if it fails but doesn't abort).
- Some items need more than a plain InstallCommand and are
  special-cased in Install() before the generic CommandFor() path:
  PHP on Windows (see WINDOWS_PHP), and Mullvad/Ventoy on Linux (see
  LINUX_EXCEPTIONS).
- util.go holds downloadFile() and runCmd(), small helpers shared by
  the special-cased installers.

i18n
----
A minimal embedded translation loader.

- All locales/*.json files are embedded at compile time via
  //go:embed.
- T(key, args...) looks up key in the current language, falls back
  to English if missing, and returns the raw key if even English
  doesn't have it (so you always get *something* printed, never a
  crash).
- SetLanguage silently falls back to English if the requested
  language isn't loaded.
